In article <1993Apr15.143104.22987@mfltd.co.uk> dnh@mfltd.co.uk writes:
>I've just been perusing the Nethack Guide to Weapons, which states 
>that tridents do d6+1 damage against small-medium creatures, and 
>3d4 against large creatures.  How on earth, then, did a hobbit hit
>me with a trident, doing *13* points of damage (killing me in the
>process, I might add) ?

Monsters without weapons do damage.  I think that the weapon damage is
added onto normal weaponless monster damage.  This is why a dwarf lord
with a mattock can do 50 points of damage in a single round.

